{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Who trains</b> — habituates. Like רִגְלֵי ( habituating to ) evil, מַדְבֵּר ( training )." "<b>And Your arms go down</b> — each one of my arms, like בָּנוֹת צְעָדָה עֲלֵי שׁוֹר (the daughters tread upon the ox), and the vav is a root letter, like וַתְּנַחֲתֵ עָלַי כַּפֶּכָה (and Your hand laid hold of me). And it is possible that וַתֵּרֶדְנָה is like נַחַת (descent), the nun being a sign of the nif'al binyan, and the bet of בִּזְרוֹעֹתָי is missing, like what is found in בֵּית יְהוָה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "Comment [0]: rendered the quoted Hebrew forms in script as Ibn Ezra cites them, but their exact forms are uncertain across witnesses and the grammatical argument is compressed; translated hyper-literally. Comment [1]: the final comparison 'like what is found in בֵּית י׳' likely alludes to a biblical example of a defective/missing letter but the reference is obscure; translated as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:47.751643577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}